<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lecale</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lecale is a fertile lowland district of east County Down, Northern Ireland, between Strangford Lough, Dundrum Bay and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-sea">Irish Sea</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/downpatrick">Downpatrick</a>. It was the heartland of the Dál Fiatach kings of the Ulaid and later of the Anglo-Norman earldom of Ulster, whose castles and tower houses still stand across the area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lecale.jpg" alt="Lecale" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mabuska · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lecale.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
